\f0\b0 \cf0 4/3/23\
Fixed inconsistencies in several questions that had a \'93check all that applies\'94 response pattern.  In these questions, respondents were able to select  \'93none of the above.\'94 In the Qualtrics raw data, NOTA respondents are simply missing. In earlier versions of the dataset, failure to encode NOTA responses induced NA values (instead of 0 as intended) for some derived variable. For example, when a respondent did not select any options in the 
\f2\i benefits
\f0\i0  question, their response is coded as NA. When 
\f2\i benefits 
\f0\i0 is recoded to 
\f2\i benefits_health
\f0\i0 , the non-respondent\'92s value is coded as NA instead of 0 for 
\f2\i benefits_health. 
\f0\i0 Although we do not know precisely whether a particular respondent selected \'93none of the above\'94 and Qualtrics did not record this response or whether they skipped the question, we decided to fill in all missing values as \'93NOTA\'94 to minimize missingness in recoded and derived variables. We identify 6 variables that had this problem: benefits (Q1.14), problem_exp (Q3.4), ware_benefits (Q11.6), ware_tech_direct (Q11.7), ware_tech_indirect (Q11.8), pol_activity (Q13.15). \
\
However, there are three \'93check all that applies\'94 variables (ware_ship (Q11.3), problem_help (Q3.5), surveillance (Q4.8)) where \'93none of the above\'94 was correctly coded in the raw dataset. For these variables, we did not fill in missing observations with \'93NOTA\'94 and leave NAs as they are. \
\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

